{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 36, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark traveler bold with heart aflame for Japan’s fair land beware both time and tide wait for none who shall embark upon this grand design. Lo here does thy itinerary unfold in verse most quaint where each day’s adventures do gleam and shine.\n\n**On the First Day when dawn doth break**\nAye haste thee to Narita’s port or Haneda’s gate where mighty jets do kiss the skies. Descend with care and pass through customs’ gate where eager eyes do scan each trunk and bag. Hail thy steed a train swift and sleek that bears thee forth to thou shalt stay where thou dost lay thy weary head.\n\n**The Second Day let wonders greet thee**\nArise with vigor leave thy lodging fair and tread the streets where ancient tales do dwell. To Asakusa thou must repair where Senso-ji’s spires pierce heaven’s blue. Adorn thee with paper talismans bright and bow to Buddha’s wisdom old and true. Then wander forth to Ameya-Yokocho’s lane where sushi fresh and dumplings steamed in baskets call thee near. At dusk let Sumida River’s glow enchant thee as thou dost cross the bridge of love so dear.\n\n**The Third Day let nature’s bounty show thee**\nTo Nikko’s forests thou shalt Repair where shrines of gold in cedar’s shade do stand. Walk with care upon the paths so fair and gaze upon the Kegon Falls so grand. Return in haste ere twilight’s creeping hand does steal the sun’s last rays of gold. In Tokyo’s heart where neon lights do blend with cherry blossoms in spring’s soft fold. Shinjuku’s streets shall dazzle thee with lights that dance and shops that tempt thy soul to see.\n\n**The Fourth Day let history’s echo call thee**\nTo Kyoto’s grace thou must repair where temples old and palaces of lore do dwell. At Fushimi Inari’s path thou shalt ascend through torii gates that stretch to heaven’s door. At Gion’s quarter let the geisha’s art enthrall thee with dances soft and stories told anew. Dine upon kaiseki’s feast where every bite does tell a tale of old and new.\n\n**The Fifth Day let modern marvels greet thee**\nTo Osaka’s heart thou shalt repair where Universal’s dreams and castles stand so tall. The Dotonbori’s lights shall paint the night in hues of joy and mirth. Street food’s bounty calls with takoyaki’s balls and okonomiyaki’s savory delight.\n\n**The Sixth Day let thy final feast be grand**\nTo Hiroshima’s shrine thou must repair where peace’s bell does chime for all the world. From thence to Miyajima’s island fair where torii gates do float on tides of old. Return with heart both heavy and light to Tokyo’s embrace where thy last night’s lodging doth await.\n\n**On the Seventh Day with sunrise bright**\nTo Narita or Haneda’s port thou must repair where flights of fancy bear thee ‘cross the sea. Depart with joy yet sadness too for Japan’s fair land shall forever call thee back as memories do whisper soft and true.", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.16029712557792664}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.0027155925054103136}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -3.846748113632202}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.0007453762227669358}, {"token": " bold", "logprob": -0.6849004030227661}, {"token": " with", "logprob": -2.631025791168213}, {"token": " heart", "logprob": -0.44831985235214233}, {"token": " afl", "logprob": -0.658608615398407}, {"token": "ame", "logprob": -0.0006630606367252767}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -1.135240912437439}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -1.4746086597442627}, {"token": "’s", "logprob": -0.160826176404953}, {"token": " fair", "logprob": -0.4977375268936157}, {"token": " land", "logprob": -0.8973662257194519}, {"token": " be", "logprob": -5.256479263305664}, {"token": "ware", "logprob": -1.2352324724197388}, {"token": " both", "logprob": -5.9022626876831055}, {"token": " time", "logprob": -2.4369020462036133}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.2506166398525238}, {"token": " tide", "logprob": -1.3301713466